# Configuration for `act` (nektos/act) — run the GitHub Actions
# workflow locally inside Docker.  Same toolchain image as the
# real CI: ubuntu-24.04 with the GitHub-Actions-runner overlay.
#
# Quick start (Docker must be running):
#   act -j smoke          # just the smoke job
#   act push -j full      # full job, simulating a push to main
#   act schedule          # nightly job (also requires the cron event)
#
# `-P` pins the image used for `ubuntu-latest` / `ubuntu-24.04`
# labels.  The catthehacker/ubuntu image is the de-facto choice for
# `act` — it mirrors GitHub's hosted runners more closely than the
# barebones ubuntu:24.04 (it ships preinstalled tools the workflow
# expects: docker, gh, python, etc.).
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04

# Cache action artefacts under the project dir so `act` doesn't burn
# the user's ~/.cache/act on every iteration.
--artifact-server-path /tmp/act-artifacts
